  "body": "## What is missing\n\nChip-break dips exist for lathe threading (#419). No mill path has them.\nA rigid tapping cycle (G84) gets no thread-dip support in the generators\nor in the mill posts.\n\n## Expected behaviour\n\nState in the design note whether a tapping cycle can break chips safely.\nA retract inside a formed thread can damage the thread. If a safe form\nexists, add it behind a parameter with refusal otherwise. If no safe form\nexists, record the refusal law on this issue and close it as decided.\n\n## Where this came from\n\nWork on #363 found the gap. #363 asked for lathe peck threading only.\n\nRefs #363\n",
